   103	## Operational failures and their mechanisms
   104	
   105	| Failure | Mechanism | Rule it fixed |
   106	|---|---|---|
   107	| X+ degree 3 killed with 6.7 GB resident and 22 GB free | `prlimit --as` caps reserved address space, not memory | cgroup `MemoryMax` only |
   108	| Nullity-16 producer: Singular "no more memory" at 2.5 GB | a Python helper set `RLIMIT_AS` to 4 GiB in the parent; every Singular child inherited it | a solver driver sets no address-space limit |
   109	| Orphaned Singular processes after a timeout | the outer timeout killed Python before its process-group kill ran | SIGTERM raises SystemExit; a finally block kills and reaps the group |
   110	| A 24 h E8-bar -> VB run that no deadline stopped | a deadline-extension script stopped the `timeout` supervisor with SIGSTOP | extend a deadline with a new timer or a cgroup, never by stopping the supervisor |
   111	| Session killed with every job, 2026-10-29 09:45 UTC | systemd-oomd acts on the whole user-session slice at high memory pressure | each heavy job in its own capped scope; reachable caps below physical memory |
   112	| W8 degree 2 exit 137 at 6 GB | the job's own cgroup limit | passed at 12 GB |
   113	| Kaggle TPU v5e-8 never assigned in 6 h | one batch TPU slot per account, held by a queued version the API cannot cancel | delete the queued kernel in the web UI, then push |
   114	
   115	## Hypotheses tested against the data
   116	
   117	**The fiber cone is generated by its quadric relations, F(I) = k[y]/K2.** Survives through degree 4 on E8-bar -> VB
   118	(h_4 = 155 equals the quadric value, no new relation), through degree 3 on X and Iso and through degree 2 elsewhere.
   119	If it holds in every degree, the fiber is all of V(K2) and contains the degree-3 component that no arc has reached.
   120	If the fiber were the degree-4 component alone, its Hilbert function would grow like 4d^3/6 against 7d^3/6 for
   121	k[y]/K2, so new relations must appear in some degree; none appears through degree 4.
   122	
   123	**The exceptional fiber is reduced.** Falsified for X- and E8-bar -> N+. Their radicals contain 3 and 5 linear forms
   124	outside K2, and since F(I) agrees with k[y]/K2 in degree 1, those forms are nilpotent in F(I). The reduced support lies
   125	in a P^11 (X-) and a P^15 (E8-bar -> N+). Survives for E8-bar -> VB at the level of K2. Untested for Iso and W8.
   126	
   127	**The exceptional fiber is irreducible.** Falsified for V(K2) of E8-bar -> VB (degrees 3 and 4) and of E8-bar -> N+
   128	(dimensions 4 and 3, so not even equidimensional), which also refutes the irreducible 2 x 7 scroll proposed for
   129	E8-bar -> VB. Survives for X-. Reopened for the fiber of E8-bar -> VB itself: if the degree-3 component lies outside
   130	the fiber, the fiber is the single degree-4 component.
   131	
   132	**The limiting kernel is the same along every path into Z.** Falsified: every hard fiber has projective dimension at
   133	least 3, and the nullity-8 record already found path-dependent boundary limits. The attaching datum is a family.
   134	
   135	**Sign-paired orbits have isomorphic fibers.** Survives for X+ with X- and W8 -> N+ with W8 -> N- by an explicit
   136	coordinate symmetry. The X+ quadric ideal at 32029 (`working/runs/k2struct/xp_p2.sing`, radical plus `minAssChar`)
   137	reproduces the X- structure at 32009 line for line: K2 and its radical are projective threefolds of degree 12, K2 is
   138	not radical, h = 15, 51, 122, 240 for K2 and 12, 45, 112, 225 for the radical, and the single minimal prime has
   139	projective dimension 3, degree 12 and three linear generators. For E8-bar -> N+ and N- the transport fails but the Hilbert functions agree through degree 2
   140	(21, 83); isomorphism is untested, and a structure computation on the N- quadrics decides it.
   141	
   142	**Results at 32009 hold in characteristic zero.** Survives on one degree of one pair. Falsifier: any h_d at 32029
   143	that differs from 32009; a mismatch alone shows instability, and naming the exceptional prime needs a third.
   144	
   145	**A completion by Groebner elimination fits this hardware.** Falsified for every formulation tried: pivot
   146	saturation (six stalls, up to 72 GB), candidate-ideal std, full-graph msolve, local orderings and minAss-first.
   147	Raising caps changes the wait, not the algorithm.
   148	
   149	**Order-1 arcs suffice to certify each component.** Falsified on E8-bar -> VB by the singular Jacobian over the
   150	non-reduced tangent cone; arcs on the normalization replace them.
   151	
   152	## What survives
   153	
   154	- E8-bar -> VB: the fiber contains the geometrically irreducible degree-4 three-fold, certified over F_32009 by a
   155	  dominant arc family; whether the degree-3 component belongs to it is open.
   156	- X-: one irreducible reduced support of projective dimension 3 and degree 12 inside a P^11, with 3 nilpotent linear
   157	  directions, so arcs certify only its support and the nilpotent part needs direct kernel limits.
   158	- E8-bar -> N+: non-reduced and not equidimensional at the quadric level.
   159	- Iso, W8, E8-bar -> N-: Hilbert functions through degree 3 or 2; no decomposition yet.
   160	- Exact degree-by-degree rank and arc families with exact containment checks are the working methods; every
   161	  global elimination is retired.
