    18	the exact producer check and the written argument in
    19	[the residuals record](../evidence/a5-kernel-bundles-residuals/README.md) (gate core-756). The argument:
    20	
    21	1. `G_2` acts transitively on orthonormal pairs `(a, b)` of imaginary octonions with stabilizer the `SU(2)` that fixes
    22	   the quaternion subalgebra `H = span(1, a, b, ab)` pointwise, so `V_2(R^7) = G_2 / SU(2)` and
    23	   `xi_R = G_2 x_SU(2) H^perp`.
    24	2. That `SU(2)` acts on `H^perp` by one-sided quaternion multiplication, the standard representation; its image in
    25	   `SO(4) = (S^3 x S^3) / {+-1}` is one `S^3` factor, so `pi_4(SU(2)) = Z/2` injects into
    26	   `pi_4(SO(4)) = Z/2 + Z/2`.
    27	3. Fix `a`. The fiber of `V_2(R^7) -> S^6` over `a` is the sphere `S^5 = SU(3) / SU(2)`, and `xi_R` restricted there
    28	   is `SU(3) x_SU(2) C^2`, whose clutching class is the boundary map `pi_5(S^5) -> pi_4(SU(2))` of the fibration
    29	   `SU(2) -> SU(3) -> S^5`. Since `pi_4(SU(3)) = 0`, that map is onto, so the clutching class is the generator.
    30	4. By the injection in the second item, the restriction of `xi_R` to `S^5` is a nontrivial real bundle, so `xi_R` is
    31	   actually nontrivial while stably trivial.
