../kaggle-tpu/review-codex.md:1:The cancellation cause remains unresolved. The retained evidence also corrects two central assumptions: **sampled RSS reached 209 GB, and msolve requested 224 threads**. The TPU VM merits a bounded parallel Singular test; another unrestricted msolve graph elimination has weak expected value.
../kaggle-tpu/review-codex.md:7:The launcher sets a **31,500-second solver timeout**. Its normal cleanup writes `result.json`, but the downloaded artifacts omit that receipt. A cutoff around 7,380 seconds therefore requires an explanation outside the configured solver deadline. [Launcher:52,84,99–120](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/kaggle-tpu/src/a5-e8vb-msolve-tpu.py:52), [download inventory:1–17](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/kaggle-tpu/download.log:1).
../kaggle-tpu/review-codex.md:9:The memory narrative needs correction. At elapsed 7,166 seconds, the sampler records **203,942,860 KiB RSS: 208.84 GB, or 194.50 GiB**, alongside 190.45 GB available. The final sample records 46.80 GB RSS and 352.83 GB available. The brief combines a later low-memory observation with an incorrect peak. Thirty-second sampling still leaves transient spikes and unmeasured container limits unresolved. [Samples:239,246](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/kaggle-tpu/out/samples.tsv:239), [sampling mechanism:89–95](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/kaggle-tpu/src/a5-e8vb-msolve-tpu.py:89).
../kaggle-tpu/review-codex.md:13:| Push-time timeout | Plausible; independent of `SOLVER_SECONDS` | Original save/push request and its `session_timeout_seconds`, bound to the exact version/session |
../kaggle-tpu/review-codex.md:18:| OOM | Endpoint samples provide little support; spikes remain possible | Container/kernel OOM event or provider resource-limit reason |
../kaggle-tpu/review-codex.md:20:Saved-version timeouts belong to the push request, rather than pulled metadata. Kaggle documents the 20-minute idle rule for interactive sessions. [Interfaces:55–66](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/notes/kaggle/interfaces.md:55), [captured notebook documentation:448–454](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/notes/kaggle/site/notebooks.md:448).
../kaggle-tpu/review-codex.md:24:The next authorized run should retain its push request, session identity, timeout, quota reading and hardware inventory **before computation**. Independent tasks should write completed receipts immediately. Stage files improve recoverability, but the current msolve wrapper exports neither its live basis nor pending-pair frontier.
../kaggle-tpu/review-codex.md:94:| Job | Proposed RSS threshold | Solver deadline |
../kaggle-tpu/review-codex.md:106:The simultaneous thresholds total **232 GiB**. Require at least **296 GiB available at admission**, preserving 64 GiB headroom. Use one thread per Singular process, one-second process-tree RSS sampling, a 256-GiB aggregate threshold and a 64-GiB available-memory floor. Threshold breaches should terminate the responsible process group with TERM, then KILL after ten seconds, recording the reason. RSS polling remains sampled protection; Linux `RLIMIT_RSS` supplies no hard enforcement. [Resource-limit guidance:51–65](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/runbooks/compute-flags.md:51).
../kaggle-tpu/review-codex.md:113:- Streaming per-job logs and RSS samples; immediate termination/completion receipts.
../kaggle-tpu/review-codex.md:120:**Falsifier:** reject another unchanged TPU batch if controls disagree, resource containment or retrieval fails, or the pilot yields only timeouts and previously known small results. Continued allocation should require a new certified result plus measured throughput advantage over the admitted host workload, or a useful computation whose measured working set exceeds that host budget. Include queue and setup latency in the comparison.
../codex-consult-brief.md:14:1. Kaggle pack A, X+ -> N+ fiber: out of memory after the degree-2 count h2 = 51.
