../decision-record.md:245:- 2026-10-29 Defect fixed in nullity16_rees_fibers._run_singular: an outer `timeout` shorter than the inner one killed Python before killpg, orphaning Singular (start_new_session); two orphans from Part A ran 30-45 min. Fix: SIGTERM->SystemExit plus finally-killpg, and cgroup MemoryMax scope replacing `prlimit --as`. Falsifier run (8 s outer timeout over a spinning Singular) left no process.
../decision-record.md:246:- 2026-10-29 iso_b (Iso method B, 6 h, 16G) exit 124 after pivot G_16 at ~10G RSS: fourth method-B/candidate stall; confirms the formulation finding above.
../decision-record.md:248:- 2026-10-29 Producer regeneration blocked: under the cgroup cap, E8bar->N+/- and W8->N+/- modular_rees_fiber stages exit status 14 (Singular allocation failure) at 2.5 GB peak, 83-227 s, where the self-test permits only blocked_timeout. A/B run with the prior prlimit cap is in progress to decide whether this predates the runner change.
../decision-record.md:249:- 2026-10-29 A/B: the prior prlimit runner reproduces the same status-14 exits (E8bar->N+/- 220 s, W8->N+/- 83 s, 2.5 GB peak, identical RSS under both caps), so the runner change is not the cause; the self-test's timeout-only allowance predates the 32003->32009 prime switch. Capturing Singular's output on those exits next.
../decision-record.md:250:- 2026-10-29 Root cause of the status-14 exits: the 4 GiB per-Singular cap. Singular reports 'no more memory' at 2.5 GB resident (allocator reservations exceed the cap under both prlimit and cgroup); with a 16 GiB cap all ten permitted pairs reach the 300 s timeout as the self-test expects. Producer cap set to 16 GiB (jobs run serially, GOROROBA_WORKERS=1); record regenerating.
../decision-record.md:252:- 2026-10-29 VM 2 results, fetched after the watcher deallocated it on six failed ssh polls (restart under azure-cases/vm2-fiber-b.md, deallocated again). e8_b (E8bar->N+ method B, 78G cap, 36,000 s) exit 124 after pivot G_19 at 72 GB RSS: sixth method-B stall, and the largest memory seen. w8_b (W8->N- method B) started 20:15 UTC, reached 13 GB with ~71 GB available at its last sample (1,501 s), then the VM stopped answering ssh at ~20:38 UTC. Memory did not cause the outage (growth ~0.5 GB/min, 58 GB headroom); the cause is unidentified (previous-boot kernel log held no OOM entry). w8_b is incomplete, not a stall.
